eview interfaces and private source-review tables remain additive.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; private Pi workers run no programs, imports, tests, installs, builds or scenes.\n\n1. Run the repaired coexistence test first, then source-review, readiness, repair-discovery and checked-renewal suites.\n2. Exercise pending review across restart/base changes, stale generation refusal, complete-coverage admission, legacy/incomplete results and terminal publication recovery. Verify later corrections, vetoes and coordinator holds survive retries.\n3. Run restored discovery-identity and read-only preparation tests: closed/changed targets produce no stale denial or pause; held planning retains complete context and unchanged authority, including no new pending-review state.\n4. Run neighboring protected-path/rename, automation-promotion, lifecycle diagnostic, workflow-isolation, capture/source-validation, MCP drift and Python-profile regressions. Retain strict assertions and quality/coverage baselines.\n5. Require the exact resulting head to pass Python 3.9–3.14, `py39-min` with `pip check`, both SDK profiles, lint/format/type/coverage/artifact gates and aggregate ordinary `fast-checks`. Historical ATK or companion success cannot validate new bytes.\n\n## Review, publication and completion\n\n- Refresh actual head/base and writer ownership before editing. Obtain separate independent complete plan review; material subsequent changes require renewed review.\n- Publish through the existing signed correction lifecycle, preserving the complete chronological task, questions/options/answers, resolver decisions, plans, checkpoints and source generations.\n- Obtain fresh independent complete source, companion and whole-task assessment bound to the published head, current dev base and complete task digest. Preserve genuine signature, provenance, credentials, security, veto/cancel, ownership and exact-head protected approval gates.\n- Retain the completed companion source publication at `self_host` commit `4e90c6ee0b7da8bd436c6efacb03d4a01ce9c2e0` and successful exact-commit run `39247424292`. Do not repeat those edits in ATK. Coordinator evidence acquisition remains the route for any genuinely missing companion material.\n- Source publication does not establish installation, live discovery recovery or visual acceptance. Preserve the reported five failed diagnostic images as failures. The prerequisite catalogue’s open PR #9 establishes no merge proof or new dependency; legacy migration satisfies none.\n- The coordinator continues monitoring every qualifying PR and repair successor through successful `dev` merge and required post-merge repair. Include `self_host` only for GitHub-agent functionality.\n- Retain ten workers, truthful labels including `agent:writing`, independent resolver-mediated choices, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies with complete Q&A, waiting-agent recovery, and singleton 30-minute orchestration while relevant PRs are open, with idle exit.\n- Restrict notifications to user approvals, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, releases and main merges. This correction grants no hold release, main promotion or runtime activation and does not declare #9 or the broader objective complete.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"d9c24a19fb48e0b69d3752a8bb1a84a671014cdf59a216f376bc6d1b4e444140","text":"# Repair PR #40’s lint failure while preserving resumable review\n\n## Summary\n\nApply the resolver-selected formatting correction to head `517c7926e4c73592310663d38337bdff7e632656`, against pinned dev `4a17e91b20b2683aca365f486e6217a141ef8c5b`.\n\nComplete assigned feedback and failed-job logs identify E501, PT006 and FORMAT findings in one test module. Python matrix and SDK checks passed; independent source review remains in progress. No files were edited or candidate programs executed during planning.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/repository/github_agent_readonly_preparation.py`, wrap the long assertion verifying that read-only preparation creates no source-review assignment.\n- Replace `\"kind, protocol\"` with `(\"kind\", \"protocol\")` in the unsupported-protocol parametrization. Retain all three existing cases and their values.\n- Apply canonical Ruff formatting within that module, preserving every assertion, fixture, test name and behavior.\n- Add a concise repair entry under `Unreleased` in `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, preserving history and package versions.\n- Preserve the complete PR feature: resumable independent review, durable merge exclusion, structured scene findings and recoverable publication. Retain the readiness tests, explicit correction fixture and current-dev safeguards.\n- No public APIs, controller interfaces, schemas, dependencies, workflows, compatibility floors or quality baselines change in this correction.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub; Pi workers execute no programs, imports, tests, installs, builds or scenes.\n\n- Verify Ruff lint and format checks report no new findings without changing baselines or suppressions.\n- Run the affected preparation module: held planning preserves context and authority; default and typed prompts retain pending assignments; unsupported protocols create neither context nor authority.\n- Run neighboring readiness, source-review and repair-discovery tests. Preserve healthy-baseline blocking cases, integration-nonblocking behavior, checked-renewal/correction/hold coexistence and terminal-publication recovery.\n- Require the resulting exact head to pass Python 3.9–3.14, `py39-min` including `pip check`, both SDK profiles, quality/type/coverage/artifact gates and aggregate ordinary `fast-checks`. Earlier results do not validate changed bytes.\n- Use existing regression suites; no additional tests are needed for this formatting-only correction.\n\n## Review, publication and standing obligations\n\n- Refresh actual head, dev base and writer ownership before editing. Obtain separate independent complete plan review; material changes require renewed review.\n- Publish through the existing signed correction lifecycle, preserving complete chronological task context, Q&A, resolver decisions, plans, checkpoints and source generations.\n- Obtain fresh independent exact-head source, companion and whole-task assessment. Preserve signature, provenance, credential, ownership, veto/cancel, hold and protected exact-head approval gates. Resolver selection approves only the strategy.\n- Retain companion publication `4e90c6ee0b7da8bd436c6efacb03d4a01ce9c2e0` and its exact-commit CI evidence. Do not repeat its edits in ATK; coordinator evidence acquisition remains responsible for missing companion material. Publication does not establish runtime activation or live recovery.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and repairs until every qualifying PR and repair successor successfully merges into dev. Include self_host changes only when they affect GitHub-agent functionality.\n- Preserve ten workers, truthful labels including `agent:writing`, resolver-mediated choices, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies with complete Q&A, waiting-agent recovery and singleton 30-minute orchestration with idle exit.\n- Restrict notifications to approvals, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, releases and main merges. This correction grants no main/runtime authority, releases no unrelated hold and establishes no completion of #9 or the broader task.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"e155ba13aed275c081f4d81faae6678f8360a64c16f6570a2b0bfbf1f3316471","text":"# Reconcile PR #40 with pinned dev while preserving resumable review\n\n## Summary\n\nReconcile PR head `675f099dbaff873cff9b06038fb60c674806ebab` with immutable dev `acc8989294a96c7b0b0d18dc257e2c810caa8764`, following the resolver-selected “Preserve both” strategy.\n\nThe complete refreshed feedback export reports successful fast checks and an **in-progress** independent review. Historical rejections retain their original head associations. No files changed or candidate programs executed during planning.\n\nObtain separate independent review of this complete plan before implementation.\n\n## Controller and review integration\n\n- In `.github/agent/controller.py`, integrate the PR’s resumable-review additions with dev’s signed local-review admission. Restore signed-policy metadata, receipt authentication, signer enrollment, original/successor provenance checks, ancestry checks and current-target revalidation.\n- After authenticating an otherwise admissible local receipt, check for **any active durable source-review assignment for that PR** before publishing local approval. If one exists, return without recording assessment or posting a successful review check. Do not retire or replace that assignment.\n- Preserve discovery’s matching pending-review handling: incompleteness alone neither creates a correction from an earlier failed review check nor triggers the completed-review shortcut. Concrete corrections, failed fast checks, conflicts, malformed metadata and provenance failures retain their existing handling.\n- Keep the real durable source-review exclusion in `ready`; successful public checks cannot bypass pending state or a current correction.\n- Retain protocol selection, progress retrieval, bundle/evidence binding and compare-and-set generation replacement interfaces. Preserve optional `prepare(..., source_protocol=None)` compatibility and validated protocol selection.\n- Preserve ordinary and coordinator read-only preparation, complete task/CI context and identity rechecks. Held read-only planning must create neither a source-review assignment nor writer authority.\n- Retain `.github/agent/source_review.py`, both schemas and the source-review prompt: immutable identities, complete substantive coverage, structured scene findings, pending legacy/incomplete results and recoverable terminal publication remain intact. Existing control tables, corrections, checked-renewal records and holds remain authoritative.\n\n## Resolve stale reversions and preserve compatibility\n\n- Reconcile individual hunks against pinned dev; do not select entire conflicting files indiscriminately.\n- Restore inherited signed local-review tooling, publication/handoff and release-preparation behavior, immutable review evidence and their regression coverage. Preserve current MCP receipt certification and source/toolchain drift checks.\n- Restore dev’s workflow split: canonical Python 3.14 tests and quality gates remain in `.github/workflows/tests.yml`; the full compatibility/minimum/SDK matrix remains in `.github/workflows/compatibility.yml`. Preserve required-workflow classifications and diagnostic-mode isolation.\n- Restore controller tracking of post-merge tests/compatibility failures, workflow-specific failure resolution, repair scopes and trusted standing-validation task authority.\n- Preserve protected renderer coverage, both rename endpoints, coordinator authority, capture/native/source-validation isolation and retained failure evidence.\n- Restore current instructions and operational documentation concerning local feature development, authenticated Telegram controls, one-way publication and paused activation. This correction does not re-enable feature intake or restart services.\n- Merge the resumable-review documentation and changelog additions additively. Restore dev history and remove the resurrected startup fragment whose entry is already folded into dev. Record this reconciliation without changing package versions.\n- Public toolkit APIs, dependencies and compatibility floors remain unchanged. Review interfaces and private tables remain additive.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub.\n\n- Add controller-level coexistence coverage in a focused source-review discovery test module, using disposable private state and fake GitHub responses:\n  - A valid local receipt with no active assignment retains dev’s admission behavior.\n  - An active assignment prevents local approval publication and remains unchanged.\n  - Matching pending review continues despite an earlier failed/completed check; repeated discovery does not invent a correction.\n  - Actual CI failures and concrete corrections still route to correction.\n  - Malformed, missing-required or invalidly signed receipts retain provenance refusal.\n- Retain and run readiness tests with valid PR identity, isolated `AGENT_STATE_DIR`, a proven healthy baseline and independent stale-base, wrong-App, failed-fast-check and `agent:writing` cases. Keep integration nonblocking and exercise the real merge guard.\n- Retain source-review generation, coverage and terminal-publication recovery tests, including preservation of later findings and holds. Keep the explicit `require_correction(..., expected=None)` coexistence fixture and full authority-row comparisons.\n- Run neighboring local-review admission, changelog folding, repair discovery, read-only preparation, coordinator, protected-path/rename, workflow-isolation and MCP drift regressions. Preserve quality and coverage baselines.\n- Require fresh exact-head ordinary `fast-checks`, lint/format/type, canonical coverage and artifact results.\n- Obtain the recorded exact-head Python 3.9–3.14, `py39-min` with `pip check`, and both SDK-profile results through the existing compatibility workflow’s manual dispatch. The coordinator must use existing authorized credentials and verify the run’s actual head SHA. The App dispatch bridge does not support compatibility; do not widen it or credentials. Unavailable authorization remains a validation blocker.\n- Preserve normal dev merge-gate classifications. Historical PR checks and companion CI cannot validate changed ATK bytes.\n\n## Review, publication and completion\n\n- Before editing, refresh assigned head/base and writer ownership through the coordinator. Material differences require renewed independent plan review.\n- Publish through the existing signed correction lifecycle, preserving the full chronological request, Q&A, resolver decisions, plans, checkpoints and source generations.\n- Require fresh independent exact-head source, companion and whole-task assessment. Preserve genuine signature, provenance, credential, ownership, veto/cancel, hold and owner-only protected approval gates. The resolver selected a strategy only.\n- Retain the completed companion publication at `self_host` commit `4e90c6ee0b7da8bd436c6efacb03d4a01ce9c2e0` and its exact-commit CI evidence. Do not repeat its edits in ATK. Missing companion evidence remains coordinator acquisition work.\n- Keep publication, installed worker generation, runtime recovery and visual acceptance distinct. Previously reported failed diagnostic images remain failures.\n- Preserve standing coordinator obligations: monitor every qualifying PR and repair successor through successful dev merge; restrict self_host relevance to GitHub-agent functionality; retain ten-worker configuration, truthful labels, resolver-mediated choices, authenticated complete GitHub/Telegram Q&A, waiting-agent recovery and singleton 30-minute/open-PR orchestration with idle exit.\n- Restrict owner notifications to approvals, Telegram-requested feature status, dev merges, releases and main merges. Runtime recovery/restarts remain subject to their separate authorized procedures. This plan releases no hold and establishes no completion of #9 or the broader task.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:68302ba1bca84a8691e7576dffd2f5cb","questions":[{"answer_index":18,"id":"aa1bc3e0576cfbbd385e0474bf6d73d151ed7d3c1d4f5a16d73c56958efd02a9","text":"Planning remains blocked by the source assignment. The assigned repository is `analytics_toolkit`; `self_host` source and its immutable current dev base are unavailable. No files changed or programs executed.\n\nI read all bound current-head check and feedback pages. PR #40’s fast checks succeed; independent review remains rejected and incomplete. The later routing decision does not prove provisioning occurred.\n\n1. **Coordinator:** Can you complete the already-selected `Karapsin/self_host` assignment and expose its source, immutable current dev base, and repository instructions for fresh planning and separate independent plan review?\n\nThe retained correction covers the relevance inventory, independent discovery cases, rename and scheduling regressions, README maintenance guidance, and task changelog fragment. Preserve PR #40’s feature/readiness changes and all standing monitoring and approval requirements. No additional owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":19,"id":"e53beb7b0408674c7febf3578919a9864c98fe8835f00285c695d438484d0e05","text":"1. Should the revised correction reconcile PR #40 with pinned dev 04945ba5c60f15eead12ccefdbfb4b7932284dc9, preserving newer dev safeguards—including visual-renderer protected approval and rename coverage—alongside the existing resumable-review feature and readiness tests, then obtain separate independent plan review?\nReconcile dev (Recommended): Retain current dev behavior and PR #40’s intended additions; review material conflicts independently and validate the resulting exact head on GitHub."}],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"implement it on your own if orchestator is not doing that","task_id":"68302ba1bca84a8691e7576dffd2f5cb","version":2}